WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:07.220
Two neighbouring cells in a chick spinal cord make the same protein.

2
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.980
One becomes a motor neuron, the other an interneuron.

3
00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:15.140
The protein is Lhx3.

4
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:19.620
Both newly born motor neurons and V2 interneurons make it.

5
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:26.060
A second protein, Isl1, is made in the motor neurons, not the V2 interneurons.

6
00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:29.140
Both are LIM homeodomain proteins.

7
00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:31.560
The homeodomain binds DNA.

8
00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:35.520
Two LIM domains are handles that other proteins grip.

9
00:00:36.533 --> 00:00:40.053
A third player, the cofactor NLI, binds no DNA.

10
00:00:40.993 --> 00:00:43.173
It pairs with itself and grips LIM domains.

11
00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:49.607
Predict. Put Lhx3 alone into chick cells without Isl1.

12
00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.307
Then put in both. Which genes come up?

13
00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.980
Alone, it turns on V2 interneuron genes, such as Chx10.

14
00:01:04.983 --> 00:01:09.623
With Isl1, it turns on motor-neuron genes, such as Mnx1.

15
00:01:10.483 --> 00:01:12.463
V2 genes are largely held down.

16
00:01:15.833 --> 00:01:20.613
Why? Without Isl1, NLI grips Lhx3 directly.

17
00:01:21.653 --> 00:01:23.413
Pairs of these units bind V2 genes.

18
00:01:26.883 --> 00:01:30.283
With Isl1 present, Isl1 grips NLI itself.

19
00:01:31.223 --> 00:01:33.623
Then it holds Lhx3 on a short segment.

20
00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:38.287
Pairs of this three part complex promote motor neuron genes.

21
00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:45.627
NLI is in both. What differs is the bridge, Isl1.

22
00:01:46.617 --> 00:01:48.857
Does any Isl1 at all give a clean switch?

23
00:01:49.857 --> 00:01:51.197
Try a simple binding model.

24
00:01:52.150 --> 00:01:57.210
With equal amounts, about a quarter of the Lhx3 still sits in the interneuron

25
00:01:57.210 --> 00:01:58.210
complex.

26
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:00.440
Less Isl1 leaves more.

27
00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:04.260
In this model, binding alone gives a mixture, not a switch.

28
00:02:05.283 --> 00:02:07.383
The model does not decide a cell's fate.

29
00:02:08.283 --> 00:02:11.943
In real cells, a downstream regulator helps lock the choice in.

30
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:14.737
Here is the one idea to carry.

31
00:02:14.737 --> 00:02:17.457
No single factor says motor neuron.

32
00:02:18.467 --> 00:02:21.267
Here, identity depends on which complexes form.

33
00:02:22.207 --> 00:02:25.327
That depends on which partners are present, and in what ratio.

34
00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:31.080
Takeaway: one protein, held by different partners, builds two different cells.
